From d8e150575224feaab825e713940894bf195a3ac5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:04:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dxmt, d3d11: A VM host waits for D3D11's compiles.

Every task scheduler of the process enlists itself, and
wait_schedulers_idle() waits until none has a task queued, waiting on
another or running (a task is counted running as it leaves the queue,
under the queue's lock). Natively, d3d11.dylib exports
MTLD3D11WaitIdle(), which a VM host calls when a guest process ends,
before it releases the process's objects: a process that ended
mid-load left pipeline compiles running whose shaders and pipelines
that release freed under the compile threads, and the host crashed.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
